    "title": "pandas.Series.dt.isocalendar — pandas 2.0.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.dt.isocalendar#\n\n- Series.dt.isocalendar()[source]#\n- Calculate year, week, and day according to the ISO 8601 standard. New in version 1.1.0. \n  - Returns\n    - DataFrame\n    - With columns year, week and day.\n See also \n  - `Timestamp.isocalendar`\n  - Function return a 3-tuple containing ISO year, week number, and weekday for the given Timestamp object.\n  - `datetime.date.isocalendar`\n  - Return a named tuple object with three components: year, week and weekday.\n Examples >>> ser = pd.to_datetime(pd.Series([\"2010-01-01\", pd.NaT])) >>> ser.dt.isocalendar() year week day 0 2009 53 5 1 <NA> <NA> <NA> >>> ser.dt.isocalendar().week 0 53 1 <NA> Name: week, dtype: UInt32",
    "markdown_length": 689,
